@startuml C4_Class_ChassisVsShimBodies
title L4 Class — chassis-native bodies vs subprocess-shim bodies\nFractal substitution made tangible: two completely different internal implementations of the same external CLI contract.

skinparam classFontSize 11
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam packageStyle frame
skinparam dpi 100

skinparam class {
    BackgroundColor<<chassis>>  #e8f5ee
    BorderColor<<chassis>>      #1c8a6a
    BackgroundColor<<body>>     #ffffff
    BorderColor<<body>>         #3366AA
    BackgroundColor<<shim>>     #e8f5ee
    BorderColor<<shim>>         #1c8a6a
    BackgroundColor<<wrapped>>  #FFE0B3
    BorderColor<<wrapped>>      #CC8800
    BackgroundColor<<composer>> #F2EAF7
    BorderColor<<composer>>     #6a4ba9
}

legend top right
  |Color|Meaning|
  |<#e8f5ee>| 🟢 NEW or chassis (created/lives in scrap, by this plan or earlier)|
  |<#ffffff>| 🔵 KEPT body — chassis-native, existed before this plan|
  |<#FFE0B3>| 🟠 WRAPPED — external script invoked by a shim|
  |<#F2EAF7>| 🟣 COMPOSER — bash orchestrator at the top|
endlegend

' --- Chassis (shared library) ---
package "agent_core.py (chassis)" {
  class AgentConfig <<chassis>> {
    + name : str
    + goal : str
    + extra_rules : str
    + session : str
    + max_steps : int
    + post_click_sleep_s : float
    + output_dir : Path
  }

  class "run_agent()" as RunAgent <<chassis>> {
    + run_agent(url, config, no_nav) : dict
  }
  AgentConfig <.. RunAgent : consumes
}

' --- Chassis-native bodies (Python files that USE agent_core) ---
package "Chassis-native bodies (Python · import agent_core)" {
  class "signup_agent.py" as Signup <<body>> {
    + GOAL : str
    + EXTRA_RULES : str
    + main() : None
  }
  class "onboarding_skipper_agent.py" as Skipper <<body>> {
    + GOAL : str
    + EXTRA_RULES : str
    + main() : None
  }
  class "onboarding_doer_agent.py" as Doer <<body>> {
    + GOAL : str
    + EXTRA_RULES : str
    + get_profile_text() : str
    + main() : None
  }
  class "get_api_agent.py" as GetApi <<body>> {
    + GOAL : str
    + EXTRA_RULES : str
    + main() : None
  }
  class "login_type_detector.py" as Detector <<shim>> {
    + main() : None
    .. uses agent_core.get_state ..
    .. NO LLM, pure regex ..
  }
}

' Chassis-native bodies instantiate AgentConfig + call run_agent
Signup ..> AgentConfig : instantiates
Signup ..> RunAgent : calls
Skipper ..> AgentConfig : instantiates
Skipper ..> RunAgent : calls
Doer ..> AgentConfig : instantiates
Doer ..> RunAgent : calls
GetApi ..> AgentConfig : instantiates
GetApi ..> RunAgent : calls

' --- Subprocess-shim bodies (Python files that DO NOT use agent_core's loop) ---
package "Subprocess-shim bodies (Python · NO agent_core loop)" {
  class "form_fill_signup_agent.py" as FormFillShim <<shim>> {
    + main() : None
    .. site dispatch: reddit | upwork | github ..
    .. subprocess.run(rung script) ..
    .. emit final-line JSON ..
  }
  class "two_fa_bypass_agent.py" as TwoFaShim <<shim>> {
    + main() : None
    .. --provider github (v1 only) ..
    .. subprocess.run(bypass_github_oauth) ..
    .. emit final-line JSON ..
  }
}

' --- Wrapped externals (browser-use scripts, lived outside scrap) ---
package "Wrapped externals (browser-use + Gemini · separate stack)" {
  class "rung_2_reddit_login.py" as Rung2 <<wrapped>> {
    + main() : None
    .. browser-use Agent ..
    .. REDDIT_GMAIL + REDDIT_PASSWORD ..
    .. ~/dev/browser-use-experiments/experiments/ ..
  }
  class "rung_4_upwork_login.py" as Rung4 <<wrapped>> {
    + main() : None
    .. browser-use Agent ..
    .. UPWORK_EMAIL + UPWORK_PASSWORD ..
  }
  class "bypass_github_oauth.py" as GhBypass <<wrapped>> {
    + main() : None
    .. browser-use Agent + pyotp ..
    .. GITHUB_* + GITHUB_TOTP_SECRET ..
    .. ~/dev/pullfrog-cli/scripts/ ..
  }
}

' Shims invoke wrapped externals via subprocess
FormFillShim ..> Rung2 : subprocess.run
FormFillShim ..> Rung4 : subprocess.run
TwoFaShim ..> GhBypass : subprocess.run

' --- Composer (bash, top-level) ---
package "Composer (bash · the role)" {
  class "login_agent.sh" as Composer <<composer>> {
    + URL → SITE (hostname switch)
    + opencli tab new
    + detector → JSON parse → switch
    + signup OR form_fill_shim
    + (post-auth) twofa_shim if 2FA
    + skipper → doer if forced-fields
    + final-line JSON {status, session}
  }
}

' Composer dispatches to every sub-agent
Composer ..> Detector : python ... --session login
Composer ..> Signup : python ... --no-nav
Composer ..> FormFillShim : python ... --site $SITE
Composer ..> TwoFaShim : python ... --provider github
Composer ..> Skipper : python ... --no-nav
Composer ..> Doer : python ... --no-nav

note bottom of Composer
  **The fractal-substitution payoff:**
  The composer doesn't care which internal shape each
  sub-agent uses. It calls them all the same way:
  subprocess → check exit code → read last-line JSON →
  branch. Chassis-native (Signup, Skipper, Doer, Detector)
  and shim-wrapped (FormFillShim, TwoFaShim) are
  indistinguishable from outside.

  v2 fan-out: each subprocess call becomes a sibling
  Paperclip role with its own parent/sub-issue. No
  sub-agent code changes.
end note

@enduml
